91411335,"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nThe Log4j fallback adds avoidable hot-path iteration, and migration notes omit removed selector properties.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open findings</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Avoid iterating MapMessage entries when capture is disabled](#discussion_r4210941371) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Document removal of source-specific include/exclude selectors](#discussion_r4210941564) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5447128387","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5447128387},{"body":"[General] This non-null fallback predicate makes `LogEventMapper.captureMessage()` iterate every `MapMessage` entry even for standalone appenders installed through `install(OpenTelemetry)` with capture left disabled; previously a null selector skipped `getData().forEach(...)` entirely. That adds per-entry predicate and atomic-read overhead to the logging hot path for users whose behavior should remain unchanged. Keep the mapper selector nullable while the default is unset, and update it when the two-argument installer supplies a selector (for example, via mutable selector state in the mapper).","comment_commit_id":"9fac7077948bd1427cadff3b45732cd5d6c5d620","comment_id":4210941371,"key":"inline:4210941371","kind":"inline","line":483,"original_commit_id":"9fac7077948bd1427cadff3b45732cd5d6c5d620","original_line":483,"path":"instrumentation/log4j/log4j-appender-2.17/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/log4j/appender/v2_17/OpenTelemetryAppender.java","review_commit_id":"9fac7077948bd1427cadff3b45732cd5d6c5d620","review_id":5447128387,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-07T19:14:19Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"5ab2f3cc5b69d830176707bbae25a5ff7066400ade018581c72b7aa14e4781cc","id":4210941371,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-07T19:14:19Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qDpUL"},{"body":"[General] This migration note only names the four deprecated boolean toggles, but this PR also removes every source-specific `.included`/`.excluded` selector. Users of those selectors will otherwise have their settings silently ignored while the new default captures all structured attributes, which can unexpectedly export keys they had filtered. Please list those removed selector families (or explicitly state that both their include and exclude properties were removed) alongside the booleans.","comment_commit_id":"9fac7077948bd1427cadff3b45732cd5d6c5d620","comment_id":4210941564,"key":"inline:4210941564","kind":"inline","line":16,"original_commit_id":"9fac7077948bd1427cadff3b45732cd5d6c5d620","original_line":16,"path":"CHANGELOG.md","review_commit_id":"9fac7077948bd1427cadff3b45732cd5d6c5d620","review_id":5447128387,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-07T19:14:19Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_i